Step 4 recording lifecycle corrective implementation — static review
Date: 2026-08-15
Scope: esp/main/wakeword.cpp, esp/main/wakeword.h, esp/main/state.cpp only

Review result: PASS — source stable for the single corrective official build.

Findings addressed:
- i2s_channel_read uses a bounded 100 ms timeout; portMAX_DELAY is absent from the listener.
- recording_started_tick uses the monotonic FreeRTOS tick; the 60 second deadline is checked after every read, including timeout/no-data paths.
- Silence completion remains SILENCE_THRESHOLD=800 with a 2500 ms silence duration.
- RecordingStatus is synchronized with a FreeRTOS portMUX and distinguishes IDLE, ACTIVE, COMPLETED, FAILED, and ABORTED.
- WAV header finalization has one call site and publishes COMPLETED only after a non-empty, in-bounds buffer is finalized.
- FAILED/ABORTED recordings return zero size and a null upload buffer; state.cpp skips upload unless status is COMPLETED with data.
- Allocation, I2S error/partial-read, and state watchdog failures return to a safe non-uploading state.
- State machine watchdog is bounded at 65000 ms and calls abort_recording on timeout.
- BMOState access is synchronized with a FreeRTOS portMUX; recording data/status accesses are synchronized with a separate portMUX.
- Progress diagnostics are rate-limited to one per second and contain only context, elapsed_ms, samples, and silence_ms. Finish/failure reasons contain no audio or credential data.

